{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Mirror inventory finding F2 (`reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md`), MEDIUM.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe op-cert kind vocabulary has three masters:\n\n- `src/rebar/signing.py:115` `OPCERT_KINDS` — canonical, and already EXPORTED in `__all__` at `:76`\n- `src/rebar/opcert_service/jobs.py:38` `VALID_KINDS` — the same two, hand-copied\n- `src/rebar/_commands/remote_cert.py:24` `_VALID_KINDS` — the same two again, plus a prose copy\n  in `_USAGE` at `:23`\n\nNeither consumer imports the exported name, and both gate client REQUEST VALIDATION: a kind\npresent in `OPCERT_KINDS` but missing from a consumer's copy is silently rejected as invalid.\nChurn is low — ADR 0049 fixes the count at two — which is precisely why a miss would sit\nunnoticed.\n\n## Approach — generate-from-canonical\n\nImport `OPCERT_KINDS` at both sites. The name is already public, so this removes two copies\nwithout adding surface. The `_USAGE` prose is generated from the same set.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: both consumers reference `signing.OPCERT_KINDS`; neither re-lists the kinds. Verified by\n      a test asserting each module's validation set is the canonical object and by the literals\n      being gone.\n- [ ] AC2: `remote_cert`'s `_USAGE` names exactly the canonical kinds, generated not re-typed.\n      Verified by a test comparing the usage text against the set.\n- [ ] AC3: a kind added to `OPCERT_KINDS` is accepted by both consumers with no further edit.\n      Verified by a test that patches the canonical set and asserts both validators follow.\n- [ ] AC4: an unknown kind is still rejected at both sites. Verified by explicit rejection tests.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"opcert or remote_cert or signing\" -q` — AC1-AC4.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788384771669715001,"uuid":"80877cc5-0b91-46a6-8218-a72540542396"}